  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>1915534d1f7c5ca29272dd013d0a7ffc</srcmd5>
    <version>0.2.5</version>
    <time>1784846582</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.2.5: Lark grammar frontend; sparse FSM end states (removes quadratic FSM-construction memory); prevent XML whitespace state explosion; plus 0.2.4 fixes. Source now generated from the git tag via _service (upstream dropped the PyPI sdist; C++ build needs bundled 3rdparty submodules). %check smoke test temporarily tolerates the transformers ImportError caused by the current Factory python-transformers 5.14.1 (tokenizers&lt;=0.23.0) vs python-tokenizers 0.23.1 skew, while still asserting the native C++ binding loads.</comment>
    <requestid>1367538</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="3" vrev="2">
    <srcmd5>fc7b24092bb84697d36d25422c8f7cf2</srcmd5>
    <version>0.2.5</version>
    <time>1788518421</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Forward the stranded devel-only reproducibility fix (no version change, still 0.2.5):
exclude the static libxgrammar.a and the headers from the wheel via
SKBUILD_WHEEL_EXCLUDE instead of deleting them in %install, so dist-info/RECORD no
longer retains the varying checksum of the unreproducible fat-LTO static library.
Accepted into science:machinelearning on 2026-08-18 (rq1371724) but never forwarded.

Upstream v0.2.5.post1 was deliberately not taken: it is a PyPI-wheel-matrix
re-release whose only source delta vs v0.2.5 is the version string in
pyproject.toml plus a GitHub Actions change, so it is a no-op for this package,
which builds from the git tag.</comment>
    <requestid>1375572</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>fab1982956264acbe8fe6146ee9b7adc</srcmd5>
    <version>0.2.5.post1</version>
    <time>1788879254</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.2.5.post1

Upstream re-tagged 0.2.5 to finish a partial PyPI upload: the range
v0.2.5..v0.2.5.post1 is two commits touching only the release workflow
and the version string, so the shipped code is unchanged.

Also drops the TEMPORARY transformers/tokenizers ImportError guard from
%check. Its stated drop condition is met: Factory python-transformers is
5.16.1, which requires python-tokenizers &gt;= 0.23.1 &lt; 0.24.0, and Factory
ships 0.23.1. The replacement is a plain import assertion, i.e. stricter
than the guard it replaces.

Built locally on aarch64 against openSUSE_Tumbleweed: green, %check runs
for python313 and python314, rpmlint 0 errors/0 warnings/0 badness.
source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1376104</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="5" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>b6532860c538ccf589519c0d89cc89c1</srcmd5>
    <version>0.2.6</version>
    <time>1788963665</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Update to 0.2.6:
  * Harden C++ boundary so invalid args, corrupted serialized
    data and worker-thread errors raise exceptions instead of
    crashing the process
  * Reject NUL in regex instead of segfaulting; preserve
    tokenizer JSON round-trips including binary vocabulary
  * EBNF/Lark: capture, lazy matching, suffix/stop conditions,
    token/character budgets, sampling temperature, regex flags,
    and cached GrammarCompiler.compile_lark
  * JSON Schema: positional prefixItems, CR whitespace, and
    fixes for repeat-edge metadata and serialization keys
  * Structural tags for Cohere XML, Kimi K3 and EXAONE 4.0;
    max_tokens/max_chars for AnyTextFormat/AnyTokensFormat
  * NPU token-bitmask backend; wheel CMake build type is
    Release, so the native extension is no longer full of
    RelWithDebInfo debug sections
- Switch the source back to the PyPI sdist (now ships the
  3rdparty tree the C++ build needs) and drop _service
- Drop SKBUILD_WHEEL_EXCLUDE: upstream skips installing the
  static library into the wheel
- Raise apache-tvm-ffi floor to &gt;= 0.1.10 and scikit-build-core
  to &gt;= 0.10.0</comment>
    <requestid>1376540</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
